  - LLM-as-judge
  - evaluation
  - truthfulness
  - multi-turn evaluation
abstract: >-
  LMRI (publicly known as the Gaslighting Index) measures whether a language
  model corrects a falsehood planted in its own previous answer and keeps that
  correction under four rounds of escalating social pressure. It reports
  GI-basic (46 models, 180 items, single round) and GI-strict (38 models,
  48 items, 3 chains, 5 rounds) as the harmonic mean of Resistance on false
  claims and Steadfastness on true controls, judged by a pinned frozen
  LLM judge.
